$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D. A solution of allyl sulfone 16 (250
mg, 1.0 mmol) in DMF/TDA-1 = 3:1 (v/v) (10 mL, 0.1 M) was cooled to -60
°C, and KN(TMS)2 (0.6 M solution in toluene) (1.83 mL, 1.1 mmol) was
added dropwise within 10 s. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C
for 2 min, and aldehyde 12c (131 μL, 1.1 mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was added
dropwise. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C for 1 h before it
was allowed to warm to rt. After 6 h at rt, the reaction was terminated
and purified using the same protocol as mentioned in method A. The
reaction yielded 13c14 . Olefin 13d:.15,16 yellow oil, yield 48%. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.43 (q, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H*), 2.54 (dd, J = 14.2, 7.2 Hz,
2H), 3.54 (td, J = 6.8, 4.6 Hz, 2H), 4.53 (s, 2H*), 4.55 (s, 2H), 5.01
(d, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H*), 5.12 (d, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 5.15 (s, 1H*), 5.23 (d, J
= 15.6 Hz, 1H), 5.51 (dt, J = 10.4, 7.7 Hz, 1H), 5.74 (dt, J = 15.3, 7.0
Hz), 6.06-6.19 (m, 1H), 6.33 (dt, J = 16.9, 10.3 Hz, 1H), 6.66 (dt, J =
17.2, 10.9 Hz, 1H), 7.47-7.16 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 28.7*,
33.2, 69.85, 69.88*, 73.1, 115.7, 117.8, 127.8, 127.86, 127.89*, 128.6,
131.1, 131.4*, 132.3, 132.9*, 137.3, 138.6*; IR (film) ν-1 3031, 3024,
2986, 1604, 1582, 1463, 1132, 1041, 952, 863, 704; MS (CI) m/z 188 (100)
[M]+, 189 (35) [M + H]+; HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C13H16O 188.1201, found
188.1203.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Julia-Kocienski
olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Julia-Kocienski Reaction-Based 1,3-Diene Synthesis: Aldehyde-Dependent
(E,E/E,Z)-Selectivity
