$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure E: Preparation of
Fluorinated Allyl-amines Derived from Thymine. To a solution of
aminosulfone 6 (1 equiv), and aldehyde (1.05 equiv) at -78 °C in THF (0.1
M) was added NaHMDS (1 M in THF, 1.5 equiv). After 30 min at -78 °C, the
mixture was stirred for 1 h 30 min at 20 °C, quenched with a saturated
aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted with CH2Cl2. Combined organic
layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated
under reduced pressure. To the crude mixture of fluoroallylamine derived
from N3-benzoyl-thymine 17a-30a was added a methanolic solution of NaOH
(1% in MeOH), and the mixture was stirred 16 h at 20 °C. The solution was
neutralized by the addition of 1 N HCl and then concentrated. The crude
product was purified by flash chromatography to give amino-alkenes
17b-30b. General procedure E was followed with aminosulfone 6 (200 mg,
0.42 mmol, 1 equiv), p-methoxybenzaldehyde (54 μL, 0.44 mmol, 1.05 equiv)
and NaHMDS (1 M in THF, 0.63 mL, 0.63 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in THF (4 mL). The
crude mixture was treated with a solution of NaOH in MeOH (5 mL). The
purification by flash chromatography (pentane/AcOEt, 4:6).
(Z/E)-1-[6-(Benzyloxy)-2-fluorohex-2-en-1-yl]-5-methyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydropyrimidine-2,4-dione
(28b). General procedure E was followed with aminosulfone 6 (600 mg, 1.27
mmol, 1 equiv), 4-(benzyloxy)-butanal (237 mg, 1.33 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and
NaHMDS (1 M in THF, 1.90 mL, 1.90 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in THF (13 mL). The
crude mixture was treated with a solution of NaOH in MeOH (13 mL). The
purification by flash chromatography (pentane/AcOEt, 1:1) afforded
compound 28b (249 mg, 59%) as a white solid (E/Z = 30:70). (Z)-28b: mp 88
°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.28 (sbr, 1H), 7.36-7.26 (m, 5H), 7.00 (s,
1H), 4.96 (dt, 3JHFtrans = 36.3 Hz, 3JHH = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 4.49 (s, 2H),
4.34 (d, 3JHF = 16.8 Hz, 2H), 3.47 (t, 3JHH = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 2.22 (q, 3JHH
= 7.3 Hz, 2H), 1.91 (s, 3H), 1.70 (quint, 3JHH = 7.3 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 164.0, 152.6 (d, 1JCF = 253.6 Hz), 150.6, 139.2,
138.4, 128.3 (2C), 127.6 (2C), 127.5, 111.2 (d, 2JCF = 13.1 Hz), 111.1,
72.9, 69.4, 47.7 (d, 2JCF = 30.8 Hz), 28.9, 20.5 (d, 3JCF = 4.0 Hz),
12.3; 19F NMR (CDCl3, 376 MHz) δ -117.6 (dt, 3JFHtrans = 36.3 Hz, 3JFH =
16.8 Hz, 1F); MS (ESI) m/z 333 [M + H]+ (100); HRMS (ESI) m/z [M + H]+
calcd for C18H22FN2O3 333.1614, found 333.1612. (E)-28b: mp 88 °C. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 9.59 (sbr, 1H), 7.36-7.26 (m, 5H), 7.01 (s, 1H), 5.35
(dt, 3JHFcis = 20.6 Hz, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.49 (s, 2H), 4.44 (d, 3JHF =
20.3 Hz, 2H), 3.50 (t, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.25 (q, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 2H),
1.90 (s, 3H), 1.72 (quint, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ
164.2, 152.9 (d, 1JCF = 246.3 Hz), 150.7, 139.5, 138.3, 128.3 (2C), 127.6
(2C), 127.5, 111.5 (d, 2JCF = 18.5 Hz), 110.9, 72.8, 68.9, 43.7 (d, 2JCF
= 28.5 Hz), 29.4 (d, 4JCF = 2.1 Hz), 21.9 (d, 3JCF = 7.8 Hz), 12.3; 19F
NMR (CDCl3, 376 MHz) δ -111.4 (dt, 3JFH = 20.6 Hz, 3JFHcis = 20.3 Hz,
1F); MS (ESI) m/z 333[M + H] + (100); HRMS (ESI) m/z [M + H]+ calcd for
C18H22FN2O3 333.1614, found 333.1612.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, modified Julia reaction (stage 3)
