$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D. A solution of allyl sulfone 16 (250
mg, 1.0 mmol) in DMF/TDA-1 = 3:1 (v/v) (10 mL, 0.1 M) was cooled to -60
°C, and KN(TMS)2 (0.6 M solution in toluene) (1.83 mL, 1.1 mmol) was
added dropwise within 10 s. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C
for 2 min, and aldehyde 12c (131 μL, 1.1 mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was added
dropwise. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C for 1 h before it
was allowed to warm to rt. After 6 h at rt, the reaction was terminated
and purified using the same protocol as mentioned in method A. The
reaction yielded 13c14 . Table 3, entry 64, product 13c, yield 42%. 1H
NMR15 (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.45 (dd, J = 15.1, 7.2 Hz, 2H*), 2.55 (dd, J =
15.3, 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.67-2.80 (m, 2H), 5.01 (d, J = 9.7 Hz, 1H*), 5.12 (d,
J = 10.0 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (dd, J = 16.9, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 5.53 (dt, J = 10.5,
7.7 Hz, 1H), 5.79 (dt, J = 15.1, 7.1 Hz, 1H*), 6.06 (t, J = 10.9 Hz, 1H),
6.15 (dd, J = 15.1, 10.4 Hz, 1H*), 6.35 (dt, J = 16.9, 10.2 Hz, 1H*),
6.65 (dtd, J = 16.9, 10.6, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.15-7.26 (m, 3H), 7.28-7.37 (m,
2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 29.8, 34.6*, 35.8*, 36.0, 115.4*, 117.5,
126.1, 128.5, 128.6, 129.9, 131.6 (E), 131.8, 132.3, 134.5, 137.4, 141.9,
142.0*; IR (film) ν-1 3031, 2956, 2887, 1524, 1487, 1334, 1001, 906, 800,
746, 702; MS (EI) m/z 158 (14) [M+], 143 (6), 117 (32), 91 (100), 65
(12); HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C12H14 158.1090, found 158.1094.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Julia-Silvestre
olefination, optimization study (optimized on reagent, reaction
temperature and solvent)
