$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM EVE-protected alkene acetal 6. A flame-dried round-bottomed flask was
charged with Wittig salt 5 (2.70 g, 5.39 mmol); anhydrous benzene (5.0
mL) was added and then pumped off under full vacuum with a warm-water
bath. Addition of benzene/pumping was repeated 3 more times. THF (13 mL),
diethyl ether (7 mL), then PhLi (1.8 M in di-n-butyl ether, 3.0 mL, 5.4
mmol) were added and the reaction was stirred at RT for 30 min. The
reaction was then cooled to -78 °C and aldehyde 4 (1.16 g, 5.04 mmol) was
added to the reaction neat via syringe. Another equivalent of PhLi
solution (3.0 mL, 5.4 mmol) was added immediately after the aldehyde and
the reaction was allowed to warm to RT over 30 min. HCl (2.0 M in diethyl
ether, 2.70 mL, 5.4 mmol), then KOtBu (570 mg, 5.08 mmol) were added,
then the reaction was quenched with water (30 mL), the layers were
separated, and the aqueous was extracted with diethyl ether (2 × 30 mL).
The combined organic layers were washed with brine (30 mL) and dried over
magnesium sulphate. Column chromatography on silica gel with
EtOAc/Hexanes (1 : 4). Yield: (891 mg, 2.40 mmol, 47 %) in 80 %. E-purity
(Rf = 0.32 in 13 : 1 Hexanes: EtOAc). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz): δ
5.50-5.37 (m, 2H), 4.67 (q, 1H, J =5.5 Hz), 4.51, (t, 1H, J =5.6 Hz),
3.85 (sept, 2H, J =3.1 Hz), 3.67-3.57 (m, 4H), 2.28 (dd, 2H, J =6.5, 6.5
Hz), 1.98 (m, 2H), 1.57 (m, 2H), 1.40-1.27 (m, 16H), 1.19 (d, 6H, J =7.2
Hz), 1.13 (d, 6H, J =6.2Hz). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz): δ 133.2, 125.2,
100.5, 99.5, 67.7 (2 signals), 65.3, 60.6, 39.1, 32.7, 29.9 (2 signals),
29.5 (2 signals), 29.4, 29.1, 26.3, 23.4 (2 signals), 22.6 (2 signals),
19.9. IR (KBr windows) cm-1: 2971 (s), 2926 (s), 2847 (s), 2629 (w), 1660
(w), 1466 (s), 1310 (s), 1337 (s), 1219 (w), 1172 (s), 1099 (br, s), 1030
(br, s). HRMS (m+ + H) calcd for C22H45O4 373.3319, found 373.3320.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Wittig reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (3E)-Dodecen-12-olide, a Potential Pheromone Component of
the Emerald Ash Borer
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
