$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure C: Preparation of
Fluorinated Allyl-amines in the Presence of NaHMDS. To a solution of
fluoroaminosulfone 5-10 (1 equiv) and aldehyde (1.05 equiv) at -78 °C in
THF (0.1 M) was added NaHMDS (1 M in THF, 1.5 equiv). After 30 min at -78
°C, the mixture was stirred for 1 h 30 min at -20 °C, quenched with a
saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl and extracted with CH2Cl2. Combined
organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and
evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
flash column chromatography to give amino-alkenes 11-30a. General
procedure C was followed with aminosulfone 6 (100 mg, 0.21 mmol, 1
equiv), benzaldehyde (23 μL, 0.22 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and NaHMDS (1 M in
THF, 0.32 mL, 0.32 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in THF (2 mL). The purification by
flash chromatography (pentane/AcOEt, 6:4).
(Z/E)-3-Benzoyl-1-[7-(benzyloxy)-2-fluorohept-2-en-1-yl]-5-methyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydropyrimidine-2,4-dione
(29a). General procedure C was followed with aminosulfone 6 (100 mg, 0.21
mmol, 1 equiv), 5-(benzyloxy)-pentanal (43 mg, 0.22 mmol, 1.05 equiv) and
NaHMDS (1 M in THF, 0.32 mL, 0.32 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in THF (2 mL). The
purification by flash chromatography (pentane/AcOEt, 65:35) afforded
compound 29a (49 mg, 52%) as a colorless oil (E/Z = 29:71). (Z)-29a: 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.92-7.90 (m, 2H), 7.65-7.61 (m, 1H), 7.50-7.46
(m, 2H), 7.37-7.28 (m, 5H), 7.13 (m, 1H), 4.98 (dt, 3JHFtrans = 36.3 Hz,
3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 4.49 (s, 2H), 4.38 (d, 3JHF = 17.3 Hz, 2H), 3.47 (t,
3JHH = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 2.16 (q, 3JHH = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 1.97 (d, 4JHH = 1.1 Hz,
3H), 1.63 (quint, 3JHH = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 1.48 (quint, 3JHH = 6.3 Hz, 2H);
13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 168.8, 162.9, 152.2 (d, 1JCF = 256.0 Hz),
149.6, 139.0, 138.5, 135.0, 131.5, 130.4 (2C), 129.1 (2C), 128.3 (2C),
127.6 (2C), 127.5, 112.2 (d, 2JCF = 13.7 Hz), 111.2, 72.9, 69.9, 48.2 (d,
2JCF = 29.7 Hz), 29.2, 25.6, 23.5, 12.4; 19F NMR (CDCl3, 376 MHz) δ
-118.0 (dt, 3JFHtrans = 36.3 Hz, 3JFH = 17.3 Hz, 1F); MS (ESI) m/z 451 [M
+ H]+ (100), 329 (77), 195 (21), 105 (24), 91 (40); HRMS (ESI) m/z [M +
H]+ calcd for C26H28FN2O4 451.2033, found 451.2047. (E)-29a: 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.92-7.90 (m, 2H), 7.65-7.60 (m, 1H), 7.50-7.46 (m,
2H), 7.35-7.25 (m, 5H), 7.13 (t, 4JHH = 1.1 Hz, 1H), 5.38 (dt, 3JHFcis =
20.8 Hz, 3JHH = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 4.46 (d, 3JHF = 20.6 Hz, 2H), 4.46 (s, 2H),
3.43 (t, 3JHH = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 2.13 (q, 3JHH = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 1.96 (d, 4JHH =
1.1 Hz, 3H), 1.62-1.55 (m, 2H), 1.50-1.42 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz) δ 168.8, 163.0, 152.5 (d, 1JCF = 246.8 Hz), 149.6, 139.4, 138.5,
135.0, 131.5, 130.4 (2C), 129.1 (2C), 128.3 (2C), 127.6 (2C), 127.5,
112.4 (d, 2JCF = 18.3 Hz), 111.0, 72.9, 70.0, 44.1 (d, 2JCF = 29.7 Hz),
29.0, 26.4 (d, 4JCF = 2.3 Hz), 25.0 (d, 3JCF = 8.0 Hz), 12.4; 19F NMR
(CDCl3, 376 MHz) δ -111.7 (dt, 3JFHcis = 20.8 Hz, 3JFH = 20.6 Hz, 1F); MS
(ESI) m/z 451[M + H]+ (100), 329 (77), 195 (21), 105 (24), 91 (40); HRMS
(ESI) m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C26H28FN2O4 451.2033, found 451.2047.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, reaction can also run at 20 deg C (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Aza-Michael Access to Fluoroalkylidene Analogs of Biomolecules
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Prunier, Anais; Calata, Charlene; Legros, Julien; Maddaluno, Jacques;
Pfund, Emmanuel; Lequeux, Thierry
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(16), 8083-8097

