$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.1. General Procedure NaHMDS (1.5 equiv, 1M
or 2M in THF) was added dropwise to a solution of sulfone 6 (1 equiv) and
benzaldehyde (or 4-bromobenzaldehyde) (1.05 equiv) in THF (0.05M) at -78
°C under argon. The mixture was stirred for 30 min at -78 °C, then 3h at
room temperature, then was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by chromatography (silica, pentane/AcOEt 98:2) to
afford the corresponding fluoroalkenes. 4.2.1
(R)-1-(4-Bromophenyl)-2-fluoro-3-methylpent-1-ene (1a) The general
procedure was followed with sulfone 6h (178.6 mg, 0.62 mmol),
4-bromobenzaldehyde (121 mg, 0.65 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 465 μL, 0.93
mmol) and THF (13.2 mL). 4.2.7
(3R)-2-Fluoro-1-(4-bromophenyl)-3-(2-bromophenyl)but-1-ene (1g) The
general procedure was followed with sulfone 6j (120 mg, 0.28 mmol),
4-Bromobenzaldehyde (56 mg, 0.30 mmol), NaHMDS (2M in THF, 210 μL, 0.42
mmol) and THF (8 mL). Column chromatography: Petroleum Ether 100%. Yield
of 1g as colorless oil, 52 mg (Z/E: 24/76), 49%. (Z) Isomer: IR (neat)
3061 (w), 2961 (w), 2921 (w), 2361 (s), 2326 (m), 1684 (w), 1492 (w),
1148 (w) cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.63-7.56 (m, 1H), 7.51-7.23 (m,
6H), 7.19-7.10 (m, 1H), 5.59 (d, 3JHFtrans38.5 Hz, 1H), 4.29 (dq, 3JHFall
14.0 Hz, 3JHH 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.51(d, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 162.4 (d, 2JCF 272.2), 140.8, 133.2, 132.3, 131.6, 130.1
(d, 4JCF 8.8 Hz), 128.6, 128.1, 127.9, 124.6, 120.7, 105.6 (d, 2JCF 8.9),
42.2 (d, 2JCF 26.4), 18.1 (d, 3JCF 4.4 Hz) ppm. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3)
δ -102.7 (dd, 3JFHtrans 38.7 Hz, 3JFHall12.9 Hz). MS (EI) (m/z) 382.0,
383.9 and 386 ((M)+., 46, 1:2:1 ratio). HRMS (EI) for C16H13F79Br2
(M).+calcd 381.93680, found 381.93767. (E) Isomer: IR (neat) 3060 (br,
w), 2970 (w), 2926 (br, w), 2362 (s), 2337 (m), 1671 (m), 1484 (m), 1149
(s) cm-1. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.58 (d, 3JHH8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.57 (d,
3JHH 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (d, 3JHH 38.9 Hz, 2H), 7.33 (apparent t, 3JHH=7.1
Hz, 1H), 7.13 (apparent td, 3JHH 7.6 Hz, 4JHH 0.8 Hz, 1H), 6.99 (d, 3JHH
8.2 Hz, 2H), 6.22 (d, 3JHFcis 21.7 Hz, 1H), 4.47 (dq, 3JHF 30.4 Hz, 3JHH
7.1 Hz, 1H), 1.50 (d, 3JHH 7.1 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3)
162.7 (d, 2JCF 259.1 Hz), 141.5 (d, 3JCF 2.9 Hz), 133.1, 132.6 (d, 3JCF
13.2 Hz), 131.6 (2C), 130.2 (2C), 128.7 (d, 4JCF 2.9 Hz), 128.5, 128.1,
123.4, 120.9, 107.9 (d, 2JCF 27.8 Hz), 38.2 (d, 2JCF 23.4 Hz), 18.1 (d,
3JCF 4.4 Hz) ppm. 19F NMR (282 MHz, CDCl3) δ -105.2 (dd, 3JHFall 30.1 Hz,
3JHFcis 21.5 Hz) ppm. MS (EI) (m/z) 382.0, 384.0 and 386.0 ((M)+., 45,
1:2:1 ratio). HRMS (EI) for C16H13F79Br2 (M).+calcd 381.93680, found
381.93750.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
