$DATUM Methyl
2-((2R,6S)-6-((2E,4E,6S,8E,10S,11R,12R)-12-((tert-butyldimethylsilyl)oxy)-11-methoxy-6,8,10-trimethyltrideca-2,4,8-trien-2-yl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)acetate
(20b). A stirred solution of sulfone 19 (293 mg, 0.54 mmol) in anhydrous
THF (1.5 mL) was cooled to - 78 °C (bath temperature) and slowly treated
with a solution of KHMDS (0.5 mL, 0.5 M in toluene). The solution turned
to yellow and was allowed to stir for 1 hour. This solution was slowly
treated with a solution of aldehyde 16b (95 mg, 044 mmol) in anhydrous
THF (0.8 mL). The resulting reaction solution was allowed to stir at this
temperature for 2 h and then quenched by the addition of saturated
aqueous NH4Cl (3 mL). The mixture was allowed to warm to rt and stir for
15 min. The aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL), and the
organic phases were washed with brine (5 mL) and dried (Na2SO4). This was
concentrated and the residue was purified on silica gel (2-20% EtOAc in
hexanes). 95 mg (45%, or 65% based on the recovered sulfone) of triene
20b as an inseparable mixture of E and Z isomers (7:2) as an oil. [α]D =
-12.0 (c = 1.4, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.19 (ddd, J = 15.2,
10.8, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.00 - 5.93 (m, 1H), 5.56 (dd, J = 15.1, 7.5 Hz, 1H),
5.17 - 5.10 (m, 1H), 3.87 - 3.78 (m, 2H), 3.76 - 3.70 (m, 1H), 3.67 (s,
3H), 3.44 (s, 3H), 2.78 (m, 1H), 2.65 - 2.50 (m, 2H), 2.48 - 2.34 (m,
2H), 2.04 - 1.98 (m, 1H), 1.96 - 1.83 (m, 2H), 1.72 (d, J = 1.4 Hz, 3H),
1.67 - 1.54 (m, 6H), 1.30 - 1.20 (m, 2H), 1.12 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 0.99
- 0.92 (m, 3H), 0.93 - 0.85 (m, 12H), 0.06 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 171.8, 140.4, 136.0, 131.5, 130.9, 124.7, 123.9, 89.8, 82.3,
74.3, 70.1, 60.8, 51.5, 47.5, 41.5, 35.0, 33.7, 31.0, 29.5, 25.9 (3C),
23.5, 20.2, 20.0, 18.1, 16.1, 15.4, 13.3, -4.5, -4.5; HRMS (ESI) m/z
calcd for C31H57O5Si (M+H)+ 537.3975, found 537.3962.
