$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for 3-8. To a solution of 19
(43 mg, 0.078 mmol) in anhydrous THF (260 μL) at -50 ºC was added
dropwise LHMDS (78 μL, 1.0 M in THF, 0.078 mmol) and the mixture was
stirred at the same temperature for 2 h. Next, a solution of the
corresponding ketone 14 (23 mg, 0.047 mmol) in anhydrous THF (310 μL) was
added dropwise to the mixture. After being stirred at -50 ºC during 5 h,
the reaction mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous solution of
NH4Cl and extracted with Et2O. The combined organic fractions were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated to give a crude which was dissolved
in anhydrous MeOH (1.2 mL) and cooled down at 0 ºC. (–)- CSA (50 mg,
0.220 mmol) was then added, and the mixture was stirred a room
temperature overnight. The reaction was quenched by adding a saturated
aqueous solution of NaHCO3. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc.
The combined organic fractions were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated to give a crude which was purified by column chromatography
using silica gel 60 Å (32-63 μm) pH 7 and EtOAc as eluent. The
diastereoisomers were isolated by reversephase preparative HPLC (ODS-A
column, 5 μm, 250x10 mm). Conditions: 4.5 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O (45:55) for 3
and 4; 4 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O (50:50) for 5 and 6. Retention times: t R (3)=
28.6 min. t R (4)= 24.1 min. t R (5)= 20.7 min. t R (6)= 18.9 min.
1α,2α,25-Trihydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (3). Yield: 52%.
1α,2α-Epoxy-25-hydroxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (9) and
2β,3β-Epoxy-1α,25-dihydroxy-3- deoxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (10). To a
solution of 19 (40 mg, 0.074 mmol) in anhydrous THF (250 μL) at -50 ºC
was added dropwise LHMDS (74 μL 1.0 M in THF, 0.074 mmol) and the mixture
was stirred at the same temperature for 2 h. Next, a solution of the
ketone 27 (20 mg, 0.044 mmol) in anhydrous THF (300 μL) was added
dropwise to the mixture. After being stirred at -50 ºC during 5 h, the
reaction mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl
and extracted with Et2O. The combined organic fractions were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated to give a crude which was dissolved
in anhydrous MeOH (1.2 mL) and cooled down at 0 ºC. (–)-CSA (50 mg, 0.220
mmol) was then added, and the mixture was stirred a room temperature
overnight. The reaction was quenched by adding a saturated aqueous
solution of NaHCO3. The aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc, the
combined organic fractions were dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
concentrated. To a solution of the crude residue in anhydrous THF (500
μL) was added dropwise DBU (10 μl, 0.066 mmol) and the reaction was
stirred at room temperature for 16 h. Solvent was concentrated and the
crude was purified by column chromatography using silica gel 60 Å (32-63
μm) pH 7 and 10% hexane/EtOAc as eluent. The diastereoisomer mixture was
separated by reverse-phase preparative HPLC (ODS-A column, 5 μm, 250x10
mm, 5 mL/min, CH3CN/H2O 65:35). Retention times: t R (9)= 20.4 min. t R
(10)= 23.4 min. (9):Yield: 20%. (10):Yield: 34%. Data for 9:tR: 1H NMR
(600.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.60 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.96 (d, 3H,Me 21, 3 J HH 6.8
Hz), 1.09 (m, 1H), 1.24 (s, 6H, Me 26+Me 27), 1.25 – 1.7 (m, 16H), 1.93
(m, 1H), 2.05 (m, 2H), 2.10 (dd, 1H, H4ax, |2 J HH| 18.1, 3 J HH 3.8 Hz),
2.69 (d, 1H, H4e, |2 J HH| 14.3 Hz), 2.75 (d, 1H, H10a, |2 J HH|
18.1,Hz), 2.80 (dd, 1H, H9e, |2 J HH| 12.8, 3 J HH 4.6 Hz), 2.91 (dd, 1H,
H10e, 2 J HH| 18.2, 3 J HH 3.8 Hz), 3.22 (s, 1H, H2), 3.30 (m, 1H, H1),
4.31 (s, 1H, H3), 5.77 (d, 1H, H7, 3 J HH 11.3 Hz) and 6.18 (d, 1H, H6, 3
J HH 11.3 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (150.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ 12.1 (CH3), 18.8 (CH3),
20.8 (CH2), 22.2 (CH2), 23.5 (CH2), 26.3 (CH2), 27.6 (CH2), 29.0 (C9),
29.2 (Me 26), 29.4 (Me 27), 36.1 (CH), 36.4 (CH2), 38.2 (CH2), 40.5
(CH2), 44.4 (CH2), 45.8 (C), 52.5 (C1), 54.6 (C2), 56.3 (CH), 56.5 (CH),
66.5 (C3), 71.1 (C),115.1 (C7), 124.1 (C6), 126.8 (C5) and 143.5 (C8)
ppm; MS (EI+, m/z): 402 [M+, 12%], 384 [(M−H20)+, 10%], 348 (24), 237
(52), 133 (55) and 91 (100). HRMS (EI+, m/z) calculated for C26H42O3
(M+): 402.3129. Found: 402.3130. Data for 10: 1H NMR (600.13 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 0.55 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.95 (d, 3H, Me 21, 3 J HH 6.4 Hz), 1.08 (m, 1H),
1.24 (s, 6H, Me 26+Me 27), 1.25 – 1.7 (m, 15H), 1.80 (m, 1H), 1.92 (m,
1H), 2.04 (m, 2H), 2.42 (dd, 1H, H10ax, |2 J HH| 13.7, 3 J HH 5.6 Hz),
2.59 (dd, 1H, H10e, |2 J HH| 13.4, 3 J HH 4.0 Hz), 2.64 (dd, 1H, H4e, |2
J HH| 16.7, 3 J HH 3.2Hz), 2.79 (dd, 1H, H9e, |2 J HH| 12.5, 3 J HH 4.7
Hz), 2.80 (d, 1H, H4a, 2 J HH| 16.7 Hz), 3.19 (m, 1H, H2), 3.30 (dd, 1H,
H3, 3 J HH 3.5, 3.5 Hz), 4.25 (s, 1H, H1), 5.80 (d, 1H, H7, 3 J HH 11.3
Hz) and 6.36 (d, 1H, H6, 3 J HH 11.1 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (150.5 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 12.0 (C18), 19.1 (C21), 20.8 (CH2), 22.2 (CH2), 23.5 (CH2), 27.6 (CH2),
28.9 (C9), 29.2 (C26), 29.4 (C27), 31.3 (CH2), 34.3 (CH2), 36.0 (CH),
36.4 (CH2), 40.4 (CH2), 44.4 (CH2), 45.8 (C), 53.6 (C3), 55.1 (C2), 56.3
(CH), 56.5 (CH), 66.9 (C1), 71.1 (C), 114.9 (C7), 124.3 (C6), 127.4 (C5)
and 143.3 (C8) ppm; MS (EI+, m/z): 402 [M+, 10%], 384 [(M−H20)+, 6%], 348
(15), 237 (30), 91 (75), 69 (81) and 57 (100); HRMS (EI+, m/z) calculated
for C26H42O3 (M+): 402.3129. Found: 402.3130.
