$DATUM 1-((benzyloxy)methyl)-4-((R
,Z)-3-methyl-6-((2S,5S)-2-methyl-5-(2-((triethylsilyl)oxy)propan-2-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-6-((triethylsilyl)oxy)hex-2-en-1-yl)-2-nitro-1H-pyrrole
and 1-((benzyloxy)methyl)-4-((R
,E)-3-methyl-6-((2S,5S)-2-methyl-5-(2-((triethylsilyl)oxy)propan-2-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-6-((triethylsilyl)oxy)hex-2-en-1-yl)-2-nitro-1H-pyrrole
(E- and Z-7a): To a solution of sulfone 9 (544 mg, 0.82 mmol) in THF (3.0
mL) was added NaHMDS (0.94 mL, 1 M in THF, 0.94 mmol) at -78°C. After the
mixture was stirred at the same temperature for 15 min, aldehyde 14a (225
mg, 0.82 mmol) in THF (2.0 mL) was added. The reaction mixture was
naturally warmed to room temperature and stirred overnight. Then the
reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous ammonium chloride. The
mixture was extracted with EtOAc and the combined extracts were washed
with brine, dried over sodium sulfate, filtered and concentrated in
vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 50:1).
Recovered sulfone, yield 132 mg, Z isomer, yield 114 mg, 20%; and E
isomer as yellow oil, yield 127 mg, 22%. Z-7a isomer : [α]20D = -0.85 (c
4.38, CHCl3); νmax (neat)/cm-1: 3432, 2967, 2925, 2856, 1459, 1367, 1301,
1075, 740, 698; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.36-7.27 (m, 5H),7.07 (d, J = 2.4
Hz, 1H), 6.77 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 5.71 (s, 2H), 5.24-5.20 (m, 1H),4.55
(s, 2H),3.63 (dd, J = 6.14, 8.92 Hz, 1H), 3.51 (dd, J = 3.77, 7.32 Hz,
1H), 3.14 (d, J = 7.24 Hz, 2H), 2.25-2.18 (m, 1H), 2.09-2.02 (m, 1H),
1.99-1.77 (m, 3H), 1.74 (d, J = 1.42 Hz, 3H), 1.72-1.63 (m, 1H),
1.55-1.52 (m, 1H), 1.40-1.31 (m, 1H), 1.17 (s, 3H), 1.15 (s, 3H), 1.07
(s, 3H), 0.98-0.92 (m, 18H), 0.64-0.54 (m, 12H); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
138.0, 136.9, 136.6, 128.6, 128.1, 127.8, 127.0, 124.6, 121.6, 115.3,
87.2, 85.8, 78.2, 77.6, 74.1, 71.0, 34.6, 32.6, 29.7, 29.5, 27.8, 26.4,
25.5, 25.0, 23.5, 22.5, 7.1, 6.8, 5.5; m/z (ESI+) calcd for
[C39H66KN2O6Si2]+ : 753.4091 , found: 753.4067. E-7a isomer : [α]20D =
-3.15 (c 4.06, CHCl3); νmax (neat)/cm-1: 3432, 2967, 2925, 2856, 1459,
1367, 1301, 1075, 740, 698; δH (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.36-7.27 (m, 5H),
7.07 (d, J =7.24 Hz, 1H), 6.76 (d, J = 7.17 Hz, 1H), 5.72 (s, 2H),
5.29-5.25 (m, 1H), 4.56 (s, 2H), 3.63 (dd, J = 6.13 Hz, 8.7, 1H), 3.51
(dd, J = 3.28 Hz, 7.81, 1H), 3.14 (d, J = 7.13 Hz, 2H), 2.22-2.15 (m,
1H), 2.07-1.90 (m, 2H), 1.86-1.69 (m, 3H), 1.67 (s, 3H), 1.57-1.51 (m,
1H), 1.45-1.35 (m, 1H), 1.17 (s, 3H), 1.16 (s, 3H), 1.08 (s, 3H),
0.99-0.92 (m, 18H), 0.65-0.54 (m, 12H); δC (100 MHz, CDCl3): 137.8,
136.9, 128.6, 128.2, 127.8, 127.0, 124.5, 121.0, 115.3, 87.2, 85.8, 77.8,
