$DATUM (1β,2α,3β)-2,3-[2’,3’-Dimethoxybutane-2’,3’-di(yloxy)]-25-(ethoxymethyloxy)-1-hydroxy-
3-deoxy-19-nor-vitamin D3 (23) and
(1α,2β)-1,2-[2’,3’-Dimethoxybutane-2’,3’-di(yloxy)]-25-
(ethoxymethyloxy)-3-epi-19-nor-vitamin D3 (24). To a solution of 19 (15
mg, 0.027 mmol) in anhydrous THF (100 μL) at -50 ºC was added dropwise
LHMDS (27 μL, 1.0 M in THF, 0.027 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at
the same temperature for 2 h. Next, a solution of the corresponding
ketone 22 (14 mg, 0.038 mmol) in anhydrous THF (250 μL) was added
dropwise to the mixture. After being stirred at -50 ºC during 5 h, the
reaction mixture was poured into a saturated aqueous solution of NH4Cl
and extracted with Et2O. The combined organic fractions were dried
(Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated to give a crude which was dissolved
in THF (500 μL) and cooled down at 0 ºC. TBAF (81 μL, 1.0 M in hexane,
0.081 mmol) was then added, and the mixture was allowed to stir a room
temperature overnight. Solvent was concentrated and the residue was
purified by column chromatography using silica gel 60 Å (32-63 μm) pH 7
and 80% hexane/EtOAc as eluent. Yield: 44%. Major diastereoisomer (25):
1H NMR (300.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.56 (s, 3H, Me 18), 0.95 (d, 3H, Me 21, 3
J HH 6.8 Hz), 1.12 (m, 1H), 1.28 (m, 9H), 1.35 (s, 3H), 1.38 (s, 3H), 1.4
– 1.7 (m, 16H), 1.75-2.10 (m, 4H), 2.36 (m, 2H, 2H4), 2.51 (br s, 1H,
OH), 2.80 (m, 1H, H9e), 3.14 (dd, 1H, H10e, |2 J HH| 12.8, 3 J HH 3.8
Hz), 3.27 (s, 3H), 3.32 (s, 3H), 3.54 (m, 2H, H2+H3), 3.58 (m, 1H, H1),
3.63 (q, 2H, 3 J HH 6.8 Hz ), 4.77 (s, 2H), 5.82 (d, 1H, H7, 3 J HH 11.3
Hz) and 6.27 (d, 1H, H6, 3 J HH 11.3 Hz) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia olefination, 44% overall yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis, Conformational Analysis, and Biological Evaluation of
19-nor-Vitamin D3 Analogues with A-Ring Modifications
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
