$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (4-((R,E)-3-methyl-6-((2S,5S)-2-methyl-5-(2-((triethylsilyl)oxy)propan-2-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-6-((triethylsilyl)oxy)hex-2-en-1-yl)-2-nitro-1H-pyrrol-1-yl)methyl
benzoate and
(4-((R,Z)-3-methyl-6-((2S,5S)-2-methyl-5-(2-((triethylsilyl)oxy)propan-2-yl)tetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-6-((triethylsilyl)oxy)hex-2-en-1-yl)-2-nitro-1H-pyrrol-1-yl)methyl
benzoate (E- and Z-7b): To a solution of sulfone 9 (200 mg, 0.30 mmol) in
THF (2 mL) was added NaHMDS (0.33 mL, 1 M in THF, 0.33 mmol) dropwise at
-78°C. After 10 min, a solution of aldehyde 14b (86 mg, 0.3 mmol) in THF
(1 mL) was added. The mixture was then allowed to warm naturally to r.t.
overnight by maintaining the flask dipped in the dry ice/acetone bath.
The reaction was quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (2 mL),
diluted with water (20 mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3 x 25 mL). The
combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over sodium
sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc, 50:1). Recovered sulfone, yield 68 mg; Z isomer, yield 25
mg, 11%; E-isomer, yield 27 mg, 12%; and a mixture of unseparated Z/E
isomer, as yellow oil, yield 10 mg. E-7b isomer : [α]20D = -1.79 (c 4.76,
CHCl3); νmax (neat)/cm-1: 2955, 2875, 1731, 1374, 1261, 1086, 1066, 735,
