$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Benzoxy-13-(tert-butyldiphenylsilyloxy)-(4R,8S,12R)-4,8,12-trimethyl-5-(Z/E)-5-tridecene
(33). Under argon, LiHMDS (0.50 M in THF, 10.0 mL, 5.0 mmol) was added in
a dropwise fashion over 20 min to a solution of
5-[(2R)-5-benzoxy-2-methyl-pentane-1-sulfonyl]-1-phenyl-1H-tetrazole (9)
(1.93 g, 4.82 mmol) and
8-(tert-butyldiphenylsilyloxy)-(3S,7R)-3,7-dimethyl-octanal (32) (1.794
g, 4.37 mmol) in anhydrous THF (5-0 mL) at -78 &#x00B0;C. The resulting
yellow solution was stirred at -78 &#x00B0;C for 3 h and then allowed to
warm to rt overnight. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl, and the aqueous la-yer was extracted with Et2O. The organic layers
were combined, and the solvent was removed. The residue was purified by
silica gel chromatography, eluting with 1% ethyl acetate in hexane to
give 33. Oil, yield 1.79 g,70%. 1H NMR (CDCl3/TMS) &#x3B4; 7.70-7.20 (m,
15H), 5.40-5.10 (m, 2H), 4.48 (s, 2H), 3.60-3.40 (m, 4H), 2.50-1.00 (m,
15H), 1.06 (s, 9H), 1.00- 0.80 (m, 9H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) &#x3B4; 138.8,
137.5, 136.8, 135.8, 134.3, 129.6, 128.4, 127.70, 127.68, 127.6, 127.5,
127.4, 73.1, 73.0, 70.7, 69.0, 40.1, 37.04, 36.98, 36.9, 35.9, 34.9,
34.1, 33.7, 33.6, 33.3, 31.7, 27.9, 27.8, 27.0, 24.6, 24.5, 21.5, 21.2,
19.9, 19.6, 19.5, 17.1; HRMS (ESI/ APCI) calcd for C39H60NO2Si [M + NH4+]
602.4388, found 602.4393.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combined yield 70%, Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly Stereocontrolled Total Synthesis of β-D-Mannosyl
Phosphomyco-ketide: A Natural Product from Mycobacterium tuberculosis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
